<refentry xmlns="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" xmlns:svg="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" xmlns:ns3="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" xmlns:mml="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" xmlns:db="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook" version="5.0-subset Scilab" xml:id="gf_elements" xml:lang="en">

    <refnamediv>
        <refname>gf_elements</refname>
        <refpurpose>Elements of a finite field as Scilab polynomials</refpurpose>
    </refnamediv>
    <refsynopsisdiv>
        <title>Syntax</title>
        <synopsis>e = gf_elements(F)</synopsis>
    </refsynopsisdiv>
    <refsection>
        <title>Arguments</title>
        <variablelist>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>F</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>A field created by <link linkend="gf_create_field">gf_create_field</link>.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
            <varlistentry>
                <term>e</term>
                <listitem>
                    <para>Column vector of p^n Scilab polynomials in x.</para>
                </listitem>
            </varlistentry>
        </variablelist>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Description</title>
        <para><literal>gf_elements(F)</literal> returns every element of F as a polynomial in x, in the order of the element table <literal>F(4)</literal>:</para>
        <itemizedlist>
            <listitem><para>for n = 1: 0, 1, ..., p-1;</para></listitem>
            <listitem><para>for n &gt; 1: 0, then α^0, α^1, ..., α^(p^n - 2), where x stands for α.</para></listitem>
        </itemizedlist>
        <para>Use <literal>F(4)</literal> directly to get the same elements as coefficient rows, which is the form the arithmetic functions accept.</para>
    </refsection>
    <refsection>
        <title>Examples</title>
        <programlisting role="example"><![CDATA[
// GF(4): 0, 1, alpha, alpha^2 = 1 + alpha
gf_elements(gf_create_field(2, 2))

// GF(3): 0, 1, 2
gf_elements(gf_create_field(3, 1))
]]></programlisting>
    </refsection>
